Package: deb-harden-ssh
Architecture: all
Depends:
 openssh-server,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 fail2ban
Enhances:
 aide,
 auditd,
 fail2ban,
 openssh-server
Suggests:
 aide,
 auditd,
 deb-harden-audit,
 deb-harden-fim,
 lynis
Description: Hardened SSH for Debian/Ubuntu based on Lynis guidance.
 Applies secure OpenSSH defaults for both the server and client via drop-in
 configuration snippets in /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/ and /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/,
 restricts SSH access to a dedicated ssh-users system group, adds fail2ban
 protection, and includes auditd/AIDE monitoring rules for SSH. The package
 validates configuration and reloads the relevant services during install and
 purge when they are present and active.
